"p": 3,
"q": "A company sells 20,000 units at ₹50 per unit. Variable cost ₹30 per unit, fixed operating cost ₹2,00,000. Calculate contribution, EBIT and operating leverage.",
"a": "<table><tr><th>Item</th><th>₹</th></tr><tr><td>Sales (20,000 x 50)</td><td>10,00,000</td></tr><tr><td>Variable cost (20,000 x 30)</td><td>6,00,000</td></tr><tr><td><b>Contribution</b></td><td><b>4,00,000</b></td></tr><tr><td>Fixed cost</td><td>2,00,000</td></tr><tr><td><b>EBIT</b></td><td><b>2,00,000</b></td></tr></table><div class=\"formula\">DOL = Contribution / EBIT = 4,00,000 / 2,00,000 = <b>2</b></div>",
"ms": "",
