"p": 3,
"q": "A company sells 25,000 units at ₹80. Variable cost ₹45 per unit, fixed operating cost ₹4,00,000, annual interest ₹1,00,000. Calculate operating, financial and combined leverage.",
"a": "<table><tr><th>Item</th><th>₹</th></tr><tr><td>Sales (25,000 x 80)</td><td>20,00,000</td></tr><tr><td>Variable cost (25,000 x 45)</td><td>11,25,000</td></tr><tr><td><b>Contribution</b></td><td><b>8,75,000</b></td></tr><tr><td>Fixed cost</td><td>4,00,000</td></tr><tr><td><b>EBIT</b></td><td><b>4,75,000</b></td></tr><tr><td>Interest</td><td>1,00,000</td></tr><tr><td><b>EBT</b></td><td><b>3,75,000</b></td></tr></table><div class=\"formula\">DOL = 8,75,000 / 4,75,000 = <b>1.84</b>; &nbsp; DFL = 4,75,000 / 3,75,000 = <b>1.27</b>; &nbsp; DCL = <b>2.33</b></div>",
"ms": "",
