"u": "Unit III",
"t": "Cost of debt",
"p": 3,
"q": "A company issues 10% irredeemable debentures of ₹1,000 at ₹960 per debenture; flotation expenses ₹10 per debenture; tax rate 30%. Calculate before-tax and after-tax cost using net proceeds.",
"a": "<p>Interest = 10% x 1,000 = ₹100; net proceeds = 960 - 10 = ₹950.</p><div class=\"formula\">Before-tax K<sub>d</sub> = 100 / 950 x 100 = <b>10.53%</b></div><div class=\"formula\">After-tax K<sub>d</sub> = 10.53% x (1 - 0.30) = <b>7.37%</b></div>",
"ms": "",
